<Base title="About"><div class="reading"><header class="intro"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT THE NOTEBOOK</p><h1>A place to think<br/>on paper.</h1><p class="lede">An ongoing record of questions, experiments, and things worth returning to.</p></header><div class="prose"><p>This notebook brings together my interests in markets and trading, quantitative research, finance, and the way we think and learn.</p><p>I use writing to make assumptions visible, work through ideas carefully, and leave a trail I can revisit when my understanding changes.</p><h2>What belongs here</h2><p>Trade reviews sit alongside model experiments, learning notes, and reflections. Some entries are brief observations. Others are longer investigations. The label on each entry describes its form, rather than claiming that the thinking is finished.</p><h2>An open-ended practice</h2><p>The aim is to keep the questions and reasoning close to the conclusions: what I thought, why I thought it, and what might change my mind.</p><p class="margin-note">Starter about text — replace this with your own introduction before publishing.</p></div></div></Base>
